<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan Hui Shung to tender for 54,000T US soy/corn.</title>
<headline>Taiwan Hui Shung to tender for 54,000T US soy/corn.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's Hui Shung Group will tender on Thursday for 38,000 tonnes of U.S. soybeans and 16,000 tonnes of U.S. No.2 corn, traders said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>The tender specifies delivery in one shipment.</p>
<p>Hui Shung Group includes Hui Shung Agriculture and Food Corp, Eagle Food Industry and Charoen Pokphand.</p>
<p>Details for the tender are as follow:</p>
<p>  Shipment Tonne   Type  Date/Location</p>
<p>				 U.S. Gulf  Pacific N.W.</p>
<p>    One    38,000  soy   Nov 10-25  Nov 26-Dec 9</p>
<p>	     16,000  corn</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
</text>
